```javascript
function () {
    var REF = FUNCTION;
    function NAME(PARAMS) {
        return REF.apply(this, arguments);
    }
    return NAME;
})()
```

Since we use the named expression template to handle functions which have function name, we got rid of the handle iife issue.
Internal hoist function takes care potential recursive function references very well.

---

As a result, the issue with `in_prototype_assignment` has gone. ( I'm not sure, but I ran the test. )
